# Post-publish indexing SOP (GSC + Bing)

Run this **after** a content/page push to `main` when the user asks to submit indexing, or as the final step of “推上线 / publish”.

## Site facts

- Production: `https://hiddenchinatravel.com`
- Sitemap: `https://hiddenchinatravel.com/sitemap.xml`
- GSC property: prefer `https://hiddenchinatravel.com/` (URL-prefix). Domain property `sc-domain:hiddenchinatravel.com` also OK if logged in.
- Bing site: `https://hiddenchinatravel.com/`
- Do **not** rely on Google/Bing sitemap ping URLs (deprecated / often 410).

## URLs to submit

Always include:

1. The new/updated canonical page URL(s)
2. Any hub/parent pages whose content/links changed (e.g. `/transport-in-china`)

Use **no trailing slash** unless the live canonical redirects to slash. Match sitemap `<loc>`.

## Checklist

### 1. Confirm live (block until ready)

```bash
URL="https://hiddenchinatravel.com/<slug>"
# Expect HTTP 200 + expected title/H1 in HTML
curl -sI -L "$URL"
curl -s -L "$URL" | head # or rg title
# Expect URL in sitemap
curl -s -L "https://hiddenchinatravel.com/sitemap.xml" | rg "<slug>"
```

If deploy is still rolling, poll every ~8–10s (up to ~2 min).

**Cloudflare cache (common):** Origin may already have the new HTML (`?nocache=1` shows new alts / wrappers) while the canonical URL is still an old `cf-cache-status: HIT`. HTML often has long `max-age` — purge before telling the user “not live”.

Purge Custom URLs in Cloudflare Caching:
- `https://hiddenchinatravel.com/<slug>`
- `https://hiddenchinatravel.com/<slug>/` (if used)
- updated hub URLs if any

If Cloudflare serves a stale **404** while `?v=2` works, same purge.

### 2. Bing Webmaster — URL Submission

1. Open: https://www.bing.com/webmasters/submiturl?siteUrl=https://hiddenchinatravel.com/
2. Ensure the correct Microsoft account / site is selected
3. Click **Submit URLs**
4. Paste one URL per line (new page + updated hubs)
5. Submit and confirm success dialog
6. Note remaining daily quota (“Quota left for today”)

Browser automation via cursor-ide-browser is OK when already logged in.

### 3. Google Search Console — URL Inspection

1. Open GSC for `https://hiddenchinatravel.com/` (account that owns the property — not a random Google login)
2. **网址检查 / URL Inspection** → paste the live URL → Enter
3. Wait for inspection result
4. Click **请求编入索引 / Request indexing**
5. Confirm success; close dialog
6. Repeat for each priority URL (article first, then hub if needed)

Deep link pattern:

`https://search.google.com/search-console/inspect?resource_id=https%3A%2F%2Fhiddenchinatravel.com%2F`

Then paste the URL in the inspect box (query `id=` deep links are flaky).

If the browser session is on an account **without** property access, stop and ask the user to switch account — do not fake success.

If the IDE browser cannot load Google (`chrome-error://` / blank), do not retry endlessly. Hand the user this URL and the article URL to finish Request indexing:

`https://search.google.com/search-console/inspect?resource_id=https%3A%2F%2Fhiddenchinatravel.com%2F`

### Trigger phrases

When the user says any of: 推上线 / 提交索引 / 提交 GSC / Bing / 编入索引 / submit to Search Console — run this SOP after the page is live.

### 4. Report back

Tell the user:

- Live URL(s) + HTTP status
- Sitemap: yes/no
- Bing: submitted + timestamp/quota if visible
- GSC: requested indexing yes/no (or blocked by wrong account)

## Out of scope / later upgrades

- IndexNow key + API (optional automation; only if a key is already published on the site)
- Google Indexing API (needs service account; not set up by default)
- Mass re-submit of old URLs — only new/changed pages unless asked
